# IntrusionIQ React Dashboard Implementation Plan

Dashboard for IntrusionIQ. Single page. No login. Four zones.

## Proposed Changes

### Frontend Setup
- Init Vite React app in `frontend/`.
- Install Tailwind CSS v4 (`@tailwindcss/vite`, `tailwindcss`).
- Install `recharts` for industry-grade charts.
- Set Vite port to 3000 (match backend CORS).
- Clear existing stubs.

### Design System (`frontend/src/index.css` & Components)
- Tailwind CSS v4.
- Modular component-based styling (Tailwind utility classes + CSS Modules if needed).
- Modern 2026 UI: glassmorphism, vibrant accents, smooth gradients, micro-animations. Industry-grade visuals.
- Working Light and Dark theme toggle.

### API Integration & Services (`frontend/src/services/api.js`)
- Fully connect all React components to the FastAPI backend.
- `api.getHealth()` -> `GET /api/v1/health`
- `api.postPredict(file)` -> `POST /api/v1/predict`
- `api.getMetrics()` -> `GET /api/v1/metrics`
- Global error handling for network failures.

### Components (`frontend/src/components/`)
- `HealthStrip.jsx` (Zone 1)
  - `GET /api/v1/health` on mount.
  - Green if backend/model OK. Red if down. Warn user if down.
  - Includes Light/Dark theme toggle button.
- `FileUpload.jsx` (Zone 2)
  - Drag-drop area.
  - Client-side CSV check.
  - `POST /api/v1/predict` on upload.
  - Show spinner during wait. Error banner on fail.
- `SummaryCards.jsx` (Zone 3)
  - 4 cards: Total Flows, Attacks (Red), Benign (Green), Attack %.
  - Unhide post-upload.
- `ResultsPanel.jsx` (Zone 4)
  - `AttackChart.jsx`: Horizontal bar chart using Recharts (`attack_type_counts`). "Needs Review" bar included. Industry-grade styling.
  - `PredictionTable.jsx`: Scrollable table. Flow #, Prediction (color-coded), Confidence, Type. Sortable by confidence.
  - `MetricsPanel.jsx`: `GET /api/v1/metrics`. Static load. F1, Accuracy, FPR, Precision, Recall.

### App (`frontend/src/App.jsx`)
- Orchestrate state: `uploadStatus`, `healthStatus`, `predictionData`, `metricsData`.
- Assemble 4 zones.
- Guarantee full end-to-end data flow from backend API to all UI components.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- None required (Sem 6 scope).

### Manual Verification
1. Run backend (`uvicorn`).
2. Run frontend (`npm run dev`).
3. Load `http://localhost:3000`.
4. Check health strip green.
5. Upload `ml/demo_sample.csv`.
6. Verify spinner shows, then summary cards and results appear.
7. Verify metrics panel loads correct values.
8. Verify UI aesthetic fits "2026 modern design".
